  "body": "**[Original report](https://bitbucket.org/agriggio/art/issues/338) by Richard Barber (Bitbucket: [Richard Barber](https://bitbucket.org/Richard Barber), ).**\n\n----------------------------------------\n\n```\nThread 3 Crashed:\n0   libsystem_pthread.dylib                0x1851770cc ___chkstk_darwin + 60\n1   ART                                    0x1047000d4 void (anonymous namespace)::gaussVertical<float>(float**, float**, int, int, double) + 244\n2   libomp.dylib                           0x104d25ccc __kmp_invoke_microtask + 156\n3   ???                                           0x38 ???\n4   ???                                        0x20690 ???\n5   ???                             0xffff842fba000000 ???\n```\n\nIn macOS 12\\+ we are obtaining a crashed `gaussVertical()` call when saving a vertically-oriented RAW as a vertically-oriented output image. Saving the vertically-oriented raw as a horizontal image does not crash. Occurs on all vertical RAWs with any .arp which calls upon gauss.cc for example Capture Sharpening.\n\nPossibly related to [https://github.com/beep6581/RawTherapee/commit/5b2811f42b751dfdc36139e441aed10beaa66285](https://github.com/beep6581/RawTherapee/commit/5b2811f42b751dfdc36139e441aed10beaa66285)\n\n‌\n",
